\f2\fs22 Agent Jones traced the ambulance, and fumed with brick-walled impatience when he discovered the orderlies gave fake names: Dick van Dyke and Rick von Reich. Why would they bother? There is nothing beyond the reach of PAPER. Agent Jones turned up their true identities in seconds.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>That\'92s when Agent Jones slipped in an anger that moved, not by storms clouds or jagged waves, but by the deep, inky power of the ocean. He quietly drove his fingernails into his palms, and swore he wouldn\'92t swear. He made his breath even.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick and Rick were part-time PAPER contractors. Grunts. Punks Paranoia boiled Agent Jones\'92 thoughts. The company was running a side-operation on him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Or, maybe, not. Agent Jones checked the agents\'92 contract records and remuneration history: they were part-timers. The meat wagon was a side-gig for them.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>This made Agent Jones still angrier.\
