\f2\fs22 Guns are a first resort. Agent Jones corralled Rick and Dick at muzzle-point and took them to a stony, truncated-pyramid of a building known only as Truth. Inside, a receptionist allocated Agent Jones the required suite, where Truth clinicians dressed Dick and Rick in experience sheaths\'97tight,  translucent head-to-toe suits. Rick and Dick panicked, as they always do, and pulled at the thin, yet durable, film covering their faces, until clinicians restrained them on scratchy, plasti-carbon-fibre chairs. Agent Jones had demanded them for the occasion. Normally, they strapped Truth candidates into medical couches designed for extended use, but Agent Jones preferred these, his favorite interrogation chairs. Blood and tissue easily hosed off, facilitating a speedy turnover of informants during busy times. Agent Jones missed the old times of belting the crap out of a target, hoping confession would come none too soon. Sometimes, he would continue anyway. For special occasions, he still carried a chef\'92s roll, filled with gleaming stainless steel knives, saws, drills, and other devices with cutting wheels and pointy bits.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones stood behind the clinician sitting at the console while two more connected wires to the experience sheaths. The console clinician started the baseline diagnostics, and watched a pair of flat screens while Rick and Dick giggled and 
\f3\i ouched
\f2\i0  as the sheaths delivered ever more fine-tuned stimuli. Eventually, Rick and Dick started moaning. Their sheaths stretched and accommodated their tumescence.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The console clinician flicked a switch. \'91They\'92re ready for experience,\'92 she told Agent Jones.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You will cut off the pinkies.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What?\'92 The clinician clamped her dropping jaw shut and gave Agent Jones large, defiant eyes.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Cut off the pinkies.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91But they\'92re compliant,\'92 the clinician objected.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones glared.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clinician swallowed. \'91Cutting off subjects\'92 fourth fingers,\'92 she confirmed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Rick and Dick howled in gasping terror.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones snarled. Though experience induction was more effective that physical trauma\'97it could could, for example repeat the pain if the same trauma many times\'97he wished there could be blood.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Please!\'92 Dick said. \'91We said we\'92d cooperate. Just tell us what you want us to say.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Tell me about Emil Kalheri,\'92 Agent Jones said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Who?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Cut off the thumbs.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Special Agent,\'92 the clinician began.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Cut off the thumbs.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clinician shrank in her seat. \'91Cutting off subjects\'92 thumbs.\'92 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick and Rick keened and bucked against their restraints. Rick\'92s chair tipped over. Clinicians went to right it; Agent Jones waved them away. He looked upon the informants with disgust. They were already beyond useful. \'91Cut the stimuli.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Relieved, the clinician complied. Rick and Dick whimpered in the afterglow of their pain.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Ajent Jones said to them, \'91I ask about your delivery to Sunny Contemplations Funeral Home.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We make many\'97\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Sure,\'92 Dick interrupted Rick. \'91Whatever you want.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91This suit.\'92 Agent Jones pulled Emil\'92s suit coat from a bag and held it up like washing on a line.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Yes! Yes!\'92 Rick said, with a tone of hope he might escape this after all. \'91I remember the suit.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91The guy was just lying there, dead in the street,\'92 Dick added.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones contemplated, which was always hard work. \'91You stole from the body.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91No! We\'92d never rob the dead.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Burn the cocks,\'92 Agent Jones instructed the clinician.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The clinician recoiled, her hands jerked away from the console.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91No! Please! We\'92re telling the truth!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91But I think I know who could have,\'92 Rick offered. \'91That\'92s good, right? No need for roast cock-a-doodle?\'92 He giggled like a maniac.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Go on,\'92 Agent Jones said, with some disappointment.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91There was this guy, you know? A cleaner.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>A cleaner? Agent Jones ground his teeth and exhaled. There was a cleaner at Travis Teh\'92s office, and a cleaner at the scene of Emil Kalheri\'92s death?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91We didn\'92t see him at first,\'92 Dick rambled. \'91He was hiding behind the cleaning cart, kneeling over the body.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Now I think about it, he was probably rummaging through the dead man\'92s clothes.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You apprehended this cleaner?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Ah, no,\'92 Rick said, trembling. \'91We just told him to tax off. That\'92s it.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Acquiring a taste for Agent Jones\'92 brutality, the console clinician took to her controls. \'91Burning subjects\'92 penises,\'92 she confirmed, disgusted at the incompetence of these inadequate part-time contractors.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>During the extended seconds of agony screams, violent thrashing, and the fouling of sheaths, Agent Jones watched, as if from the comfort of a private box at the opera. \'91Cut the stimuli,\'92 he said, once boredom loomed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>It took Rick and Dick some time to regain their breath and regulate their sobbing.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Describe the cleaner,\'92 Agent Jones said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Eurasian male, early thirties, 1.8 tall, dark hair. Dressed in a pair of busted-arse overalls.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Describe the overalls.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Just normal overalls, dirty white, stuff in pockets, logo over the breast pocket.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Describe the logo.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I can\'92t remember. Tone Cleaning? Maybe.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones charged and threw over the second chair. \'91Let me assist your memory.\'92 He took a large needle as thick as a pencil from his pocket, and inserted it into the webbing of Dick\'92s fingers. Dick bucked, but Agent Jones held his hand firm while he twiddled the needle among sinews and blood vessels. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick screamed with primeval pain and anger. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Do you remember now?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Dick jerked and convulsed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91How about now, tax-face? Huh? Put my contract on the line will you?\'92 He stood and kicked Dick in the head. He turned on Rick.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Please,\'92 Rick cried. \'91Let me think! Please, just let me think! Super \'85 Tone\'92s Super \'85  Cleaning? No, No. SupaTones Cleaning. That\'92s it: SupaTones Cleaning Service.\'92
